'''Second Sartan Civil War''' refers to the civil war in Sarta that lasted from 1799 to 1811.

The conflict developed from long-running tensions between the royal court, the parliamentary elite, rural communities, and factions linked to [[Volisania]]. It broke out in a kingdom already shaped by estate concentration, movement restrictions, and coastal losses.

The war ended when Volisania intervened directly and placed [[Alfonso II of Sarta]] on the throne, making Sarta subordinate to Volisanian influence. The conflict killed roughly 8.5% of the population.

